together.settings.howto.description:
With this on, a "Join Co-op Mode" button appears in the bottom-right of the multiplayer character-select screen:
1. Everyone who wants in presses it — pressing it also counts as pressing the official "ready" button; 2+ players joining forms a group that shares one body
   (HP / Block / status / deck / draw pile / discard pile are all the same one);
2. Hand and energy stay separate per player (you play yours, I play mine);
3. There is no player cap, anyone can join; with only 1 player joining no group forms and that run plays as normal multiplayer;
4. Press it again (or press the official "unready" button) to leave co-op and go back to the normal ready state;
5. Once everyone is ready the game starts the run as usual;
6. Everyone can pick any character (even the same one); whose starting cards go into the shared deck is decided by "Merge starting decks" above (with it on, every echo's starting cards are merged in);
7. With this switch off, the mod stays out of your runs entirely (a normal vanilla run).
In multiplayer the host's settings win.
